@startuml component
title payment-platform - modules and how a contract travels

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "payment-platform monorepo" {
  component "person-service" as PS
  component "person-client" as PC
  component "individuals-api" as API

  artifact "person-service.yaml" as PSY
  artifact "individuals-api.yaml" as IAY
  artifact "V001, V002\nFlyway migrations" as MIG
}

database "Nexus\n(mavenLocal until it is up)" as NEXUS
artifact "com.dezxxx:person-client:1.0.0-SNAPSHOT" as PCJ

PS *-- PSY
PS *-- MIG
API *-- IAY

PSY --> PC : openApiGenerate\nDTOs + @HttpExchange
IAY --> API : openApiGenerate\nAuthApi interface only
PC --> PCJ : publish
PCJ --> NEXUS
NEXUS --> API : resolved by Maven coordinates

note bottom of API
  Never project(":person-client").
  Cross-module contracts travel as
  published artifacts, so any module
  can move to its own repository
  without a rewrite.
end note

note right of PS
  Module 1 ships no code here.
  Only the frozen contract and
  the migrations the next module
  will run.
end note

@enduml
